  "details": "After the VRChat client migrated to Unity 6, Texture2D(TextureFormat.R8) no longer behaves correctly when sampled in shaders.\n\nI verified the following:\n\nTexture2D(TextureFormat.R8) is created successfully.\n\nSetPixels() correctly stores only the red channel, confirming that the texture is truly single-channel.\n\nLoadRawTextureData() also accepts exactly 1 byte per pixel with no size mismatch.\n\nBoth SetPixels() and LoadRawTextureData() produce the same incorrect shader output.\n\nLoad(), Sample(), and tex2D() all return identical incorrect results.\n\nThis indicates that the texture data is stored correctly, but is decoded incorrectly when sampled in a shader.\n\nIn addition to the red channel becoming non-linear, the sampled green and blue channels are always returned as 1.0, even though TextureFormat.R8 only stores a single red channel. This behavior is unexpected and was not present before the Unity 6 client migration.\n\nThis behavior did not occur before the Unity 6 client migration.\n\nfirst image: old version\n\nsecond image: U6 Beta",
